<item><title>Principal Contractor - Design &amp; Construct of Prosthetics, Orthotics &amp; Podiatry Rooms at PAH</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Metro South Health is seeking a suitably qualified Principal Contractor to deliver the Princess Alexandra Hospital Prosthetics, Orthotics and Podiatry Services (POPS) Project under a Design and Construct contract. The project involves reviewing and completing the existing approximately 80% detailed design, upgrading and replacing critical workshop mechanical, electrical and associated building services infrastructure, construction of supporting plant and building works, commissioning, and handover within a live hospital environment. The upgrade will address deficiencies in existing dust extraction, fume extraction, ventilation, cooling and air balancing systems to provide a safe, compliant and fit-for-purpose clinical manufacturing environment that supports current and future operational requirements.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Metro South Hospital and Health Service<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 29/Oct/2026 10:00 AM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP528010<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Jason Lyness Email: jason.lyness@health.qld.gov.au Tel: 07 3564 0316<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 4]]></description>
