<item><title>26/27-58 Ballarat Connections - Trail Works Whitelaw Avenue</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> This project includes the construction of a shared path as part of the broader Ballarat Connections trail. The project provides a shared path link alongside Whitelaw Avenue between Doug Dean Reserve and Sutton Street. Links back into the adjacent footpath network and south into Doug Dean Reserve are is also included.<br /><br />The combined length of the proposed path connections is just over 1000m and includes five shared user raised pedestrian crossings. <br /><br />The project works include:<br /><br />•	Site establishment/ demolition <br /><br />•	Solar lighting<br /><br />•	Minor roadworks<br /><br />•	Asphalt works <br /><br />•	<br /><br />•	Concrete footpath and kerb construction <br /><br />•	Carpark extension (10 new car park spaces)<br /><br />•	Pram ramps<br /><br />•	Shared user raised pedestrian crossings<br /><br />•	Planted drainage swales<br /><br />•	Grated drainage channel<br /><br />•	Side entry pits modification and construction<br /><br />•	Grated pit modification and construction <br />...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> City of Ballarat<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 22/Oct/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP527802<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Trade, Repairs, Maint., Construction & Operation<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 7]]></description>
