<item><title>Parliament House Carpet Replacement</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Queensland Parliamentary Service (QPS) is inviting tenderers for the Parliament House Carpet Replacement Project, comprising the supply, manufacture, delivery and installation of bespoke/custom broadloom carpet within the heritage-listed Parliament House, together with the provision of furniture removal, relocation, temporary storage, protection and reinstatement services necessary to facilitate the carpet replacement works.<br /><br />To support an effective procurement and delivery approach, the project has been divided into the following two parts:<br /><br />1. Tender Package 1 (Part 1): Carpet Supply and Installation:<br /><br />Which includes:<br /><br />•	Site verification and measurement.<br /><br />•	Design development for the bespoke carpet pattern.<br /><br />•	Provision of samples for approval.<br /><br />•	Preparation of shop drawings and seam-location drawings.<br /><br />•	Removal and disposal of existing carpet and associated materials.<br /><br />•	Supply and installation of the approved ...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Queensland Parliament: Parliamentary Service<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 13/Nov/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP527757<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Products & Materials, Building Trade, Repairs, Maint., Construction & Operation, Office Related Supplies & Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 25]]></description>
