<item><title>25/26-305 Buninyong Town Hall - DDA Compliant Access</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> - Replace handrails on front steps with compliant steel handrails. The historic photographs confirm<br /><br />the existing steel pipe handrails are not original. As built there were no handrails but these are<br /><br />required to allow the continued use of the front stairs.<br /><br />- Remove concrete gate posts to widen entrance to path. These posts appear to date from the 1920s or<br /><br />later, probably contemporary with the concrete addition to the Town Hall.<br /><br />- Remove existing asphalt path and rock edging and replace with new walkway to AS1428.1<br /><br />compliant gradients. The existing path was built to provide a link between Learmonth Street and<br /><br />the rear car park, as well as the side door. It is not considered significant.<br /><br />- Construct new pergola over section of walkway.<br /><br />- Remove existing side door, widen opening and install new wider accessible door. Install new steel<br /><br />framed awning roof over new accessible entrance to provide shelter and ...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> City of Ballarat<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 22/Oct/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP527753<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Trade, Repairs, Maint., Construction & Operation<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 9]]></description>
