</item>
<item><title>Tender 10-27 Design and Construct Boardwalk Jeffery Court, Agnes Water</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Gladstone Regional Council (GRC) requires a suitably qualified Contractor to undertake the Design and Construct of an Australian-manufactured fibre-reinforced polymer (FRP) Boardwalk located along Jeffery Court, Agnes Water. The boardwalk is to be approximately 90m in length with a width varying between 2.8 - 3.2m, including handrail sections (as required) as detailed in this scope of work. The design shall insure that static electricity buildup across the boardwalk and load bearing members and foundation is adequately addressed. The contractor is responsible for the full design, RPEQ engineering certification, construction, site supervision and provision of as constructed drawings upon completion. '<br /><br />The boardwalk must be designed and built to retain the existing trees, including avoiding damage to the trunks, roots and critical root zones as defined throughout this document. The project also includes the design and installation of xeric (low-water, drought tolerant) coastal landscaping to enhance ...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Gladstone Regional Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 27/Oct/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP527175<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Trade, Repairs, Maint., Construction & Operation, Engineer, Research, Tech services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 9]]></description>
