<item><title>Statewide Waste and Recycling Infrastructure Roadmap</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Queensland government Less Landfill, More Recycling 2035: Queensland Waste Strategy identifies investing in modern infrastructure as a priority. The new Waste Strategy is backed by investment of $487 million over five years through the Waste Reduction and Recycling Activation Fund. However, investment in infrastructure requires not just State government investment, but local, federal and private sector investment as well.<br /><br />A key action of the Waste Strategy is to develop a statewide waste and recycling infrastructure plan that identifies current and future material flows, infrastructure capacity and gaps, facility locations, supply chain options, land use planning considerations and priority investment opportunities. <br /><br />In collaboration with the Department, the supplier will produce two complementary outputs: a Statewide Waste and Recycling Infrastructure Roadmap and a supporting Investment Prospectus. Together, these outputs will provide a contemporary, evidence-based framework to guid...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Dept of the Environ, Tourism, Science and Innov<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 21/Oct/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP526785<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Environmental & Heritage Services, Management Advisory Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 5]]></description>
