</item>
<item><title>Energy Savings Project – Solar Panel Installations</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Department of Primary Industries (DPI) is seeking measures to decrease its operational costs and carbon emissions associated with electricity energy consumption and improve its reputation by installing solar photovoltaic panels and systems. <br /><br />DPI is requesting quotes for the installation of eight (8) solar energy systems across five (5) sites areas across Queensland. Responses are to include a comprehensive proposal for the installation of solar energy systems, ensuring high standards of quality, safety, and efficiency. Suppliers may choose to submit responses for all sites or specific sites. Locations include:<br /><br />- Central Queensland Smart Cropping Centre, 26274 Capricorn Highway, Emerald Qld 4720<br /><br />- Central Regional Office,25 Yeppoon Road, Parkhurst Qld 4702<br /><br />- Spyglass Beef Research Facility, 46035 Gregory Developmental Road, Basalt Qld 4820 (Office Block, Continong Station and Luck Break Station)<br /><br />- Tropical Weeds Research Facility, 27-43 Natal Downs Roa...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Department of Primary Industries<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 12/Oct/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP526659<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Trade, Repairs, Maint.<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 6]]></description>
