<item><title>Heritage Consultancy Services Panel</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The City of Boroondara (the City) is located in the inner eastern suburbs of Melbourne, between 5 and 10 kilometres east of the Melbourne CBD. It is recognised as one of Victoria’s most significant heritage municipalities, containing an extensive and diverse collection of heritage places that reflect the enduring cultural heritage of the Wurundjeri Woi-wurrung people as the Traditional Owners and its colonial and multicultural history.<br /><br />Boroondara’s heritage is shaped by the enduring traditions and places of Aboriginal cultural heritage significance, natural heritage, the rich legacy of 19th century settlement and development, and the ongoing contributions of successive generations of diverse communities.<br /><br />Boroondara City Council (Council) invites submissions from suitably qualified and experienced heritage consultants for appointment to its Heritage Consultancy Services Panel.<br /><br />The Panel will comprise approximately six (6) Consultants who may be invited to submit quotations for ...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> City of Boroondara<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 09/Oct/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP526299<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Environmental & Heritage Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 2]]></description>
