<item><title>ITT2558 - Eddie De Vere Building - Internal Refurbishments</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Eddie De Vere Building is one of Sunshine Coast Council’s office facilities and currently accommodates approximately 200 SCC staff across the ground floor, mezzanine, Level 1, and Level 2. Level 3 has been deactivated for an extended period due to water infiltration issues.<br /><br />Stage 1 of this project involves a comprehensive review and repair of the roof membrane and external glazing across the building. These works are close to being completed and are a prerequisite to enabling the safe re-occupation of Level 3.<br /><br />The intention of this project is to reactivate Level 3 and fully utilise the asset, thereby maximising the overall capacity and functionality of the building.<br /><br />The works will entail demolition of existing partitions, internal doors and windows and floor coverings to levels Mezzanine, First, Second and Third. The removal and retention of or demolition of existing furniture to Levels Mezzanine and One. Installation of new partitions, internal doors and windows, floor co...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Sunshine Coast Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 06/Oct/2026 12:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP524132<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Products & Materials, Building Trade, Repairs, Maint., Construction & Operation<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 24]]></description>
