<item><title>Mid-Coast Council Scrap Metal Tender Waste Services</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> MidCoast Council is seeking an experienced scrap metal recycling contractor for a five-year contract to purchase, collect, transport, sort, process and lawfully recycle or sell ferrous and non-ferrous scrap metal and used lead-acid batteries.<br /><br />The services also include compliant on-site refrigerant recovery and degassing of refrigerators, freezers and air-conditioning equipment before collection as scrap.<br /><br />Collections will be undertaken from Council’s Waste Management Facilities at Taree, Tuncurry, Gloucester, Stroud, Bulahdelah and Tea Gardens. Standard collection requests must commence within three weeks, while a limited number of urgent requests must commence within one week.<br /><br />The Contractor will pay Council an agreed fixed percentage of the applicable published market benchmark for each material category.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> MidCoast Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 07/Oct/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP522274<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Waste Management & Landfill<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 6]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/tsi.axd?id=db08e853f3f24c3ebe9d182765ff5c92s522274se8fec92d55d7442e83a58602a4243b67s1610</link>
